The '''Dakare national football team''' ({{Lang-bw|Kooṣo Dakareed}}) represents [[Dakare]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Dakare Football Federation]] and competes as a member of the North and Central Kaftia Football Association within the [[AFA]] confederation.

Dakare are currently ranked 42nd in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]] and qualified for their second [[AFA World Cup]] at the [[2022 AFA World Cup|2022 tournament]].

== History ==

=== Early years ===
Dakare's football programme developed slowly through the late 20th century, with the national team largely competing in regional Kaftian tournaments. The establishment of the Dakare Premier League in 1994 provided a domestic foundation for player development.

=== World Cup era ===
Dakare qualified for their first World Cup in 2018, exiting at the group stage but earning praise for a disciplined defensive performance. The team's qualification for the 2022 tournament marks a second appearance and a growing reputation in Kaftian football.

